      "heading": "2. What Is the CSS Exam in Pakistan?",
      "body": "The CSS competitive examination is conducted annually by the Federal Public Service Commission (FPSC), an autonomous constitutional body established under Article 242 of the Constitution of the Islamic Republic of Pakistan and functioning under the FPSC Ordinance, 1977. The mandate of the FPSC is to conduct recruitment tests and examinations strictly on merit to select qualified candidates for civil posts in connection with the affairs of the Federation. Successful candidates are recruited into one of the 12 Federal Occupational Groups and Services based on their merit ranking, provincial/regional quotas, and personal preferences. These groups comprise: 1) Pakistan Administrative Service (PAS) — formerly known as the District Management Group (DMG), responsible for district administration, executive leadership, and federal policy execution; 2) Police Service of Pakistan (PSP) — handling law enforcement, crime prevention, intelligence, and internal security; 3) Foreign Service of Pakistan (FSP) — representing Pakistan in bilateral and multilateral diplomacy across embassies and international missions; 4) Inland Revenue Service (IRS) — responsible for domestic tax collection, income tax, and revenue administration under the Federal Board of Revenue (FBR); 5) Pakistan Customs Service (PCS) — managing international trade regulation, border customs enforcement, and anti-smuggling operations; 6) Pakistan Audit and Accounts Service (PAAS) — overseeing public expenditure auditing, financial accountability, and state accounts; 7) Information Group (IG) — handling state communications, public relations, and media management; 8) Military Lands & Cantonments Group (MLCG) — managing municipal administration and land assets across cantonment boards; 9) Commerce & Trade Group (CTG) — facilitating trade negotiations, export promotion, and commercial diplomacy; 10) Office Management Group (OMG) — serving as administrative section officers across federal ministries and divisions; 11) Postal Group (POSTG) — operating the national postal infrastructure, logistics, and financial services; and 12) Railways (Commercial & Transportation) Group (RCTG) — managing passenger, freight, and commercial operations across Pakistan Railways."
